WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.282
The first highlighted line creates a CPU

00:00:03.282 --> 00:00:06.460
array with one zero. The next line calls

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.242
cuda.to_device to copy it into GPU memory.

00:00:12.242 --> 00:00:15.102
Numba compiles this Python kernel on the

00:00:15.102 --> 00:00:18.371
CPU. CUDA loads the compiled code onto the

00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:19.597
GPU when needed.

00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:25.835
One GPU thread runs the kernel. Its

00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:28.964
argument, out, is the array we just copied

00:00:28.964 --> 00:00:30.137
into GPU memory.

00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:36.322
Both arrays contain zero. Which array will

00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:38.240
change when this line runs?

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.372
The GPU thread writes 42 to the GPU array.

00:00:48.372 --> 00:00:50.794
The CPU array still holds zero.

00:00:53.794 --> 00:00:56.397
Copy to host waits for the kernel to

00:00:56.397 --> 00:00:59.325
finish. It returns the value in a new CPU

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.301
array called result.
